# The deep node suites: the long hardening ones (canaries planted in every
# slot, structure-aware fuzz, worst-case inputs, growth ratios). npm test runs
# them as always; `npm test -- --tier=fast` leaves them out and `--tier=deep`
# runs only them (scripts/test-node.ts). One path per line, with the reason.
#
# Chosen from measurement, not by name: the files that took 60 s or more on
# the hosted Linux runner (concurrency 3) in the CI run of 2026-10-28 for
# #232, 15 files and 40 % of the node suites' time there, less ui-server (a
# core suite), plus the suites that import the two helpers whose tests took
# longest (pack-virtualization-canary-lib.ts 283 s, windows-boundary-block-cases.ts
# 129 s). Linux seconds, then hosted macOS seconds, where measured.
tests/pack-virtualization-boundary.test.ts            # 243 / 126, and the canary library
